3:05:45.229Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"[FIX_CYCLE: 1] Review findings: MUST-FIX: New AC-7 action-filter E2E test is failing (packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/triage.spec.ts:167, page.reload ERR_CONNECTION_REFUSED). PR #619 reviewed and commented inline; worker should stabilize this test and resubmit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1G6\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Web UI triage page: add filter controls for triage action types (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, d\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJKN8H\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T02:57:23.625Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Submitted for review in PR #619: https://github.com/kynetic-ai/kynetic-spec/pull/619 (branch feat/triage-action-filter, commit e8371171a). Implemented triage action filter UI + logic and AC-7 E2E coverage updates.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"task_ref\": \"01KJDQ1G6\",\n      \"task_title\": \"Web UI triage page: add filter controls for triage action types (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, d\",\n      \"task_status\": \"completed\",\n      \"note_ulid\": \"01KJKN5G\",\n      \"created_at\": \"2026-03-01T02:55:45.072Z\",\n      \"author\": \"Jacob Chapel\",\n      \"content\": \"Verification summary after implementation:\\n\\n- Targeted AC-7 E2E checks pass:\\n  - `npm run build && npx playwright test tests/e2e/triage.spec.ts -g \\\"displays filter controls and progress count|action filter narrows cards by triage action and resets card index\\\"`\\n  - Result: 2 passed.\\n- Full triage.spec run still has pre-existing failures unrelated to this change (real-time progress assertion and submit-enabled expectation paths).\\n- Full repo test run has a pre-existing failing file:\\n  - `tests/cli/session-note-limit.test.ts` (3 timeout failures at lines 34, 70, 104).\\n- `kspec validate` still fails with pre-existing project-wide schema/reference/alignment/completeness issues (missing observations skill file, duplicate @observations slug, many baseline alignment warnings).\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"active_todos\": [],\n  \"ready_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJGDR9\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Fix ralph session-budget-integration test timeouts\",\n      \"description\": \"2 tests failing in tests/ralph/session-budget-integration.test.ts: (1) ralph loop times out waiting for completion marker, (2) output doesn't contain expected 'Iteration failed' string. These are race conditions or mock issues in the ralph loop test harness, not version bump related. Originally bundled in @01KJDSXEME66TYKVVGGFW6PYT2 which was cancelled after the version-bump failures resolved themselves.\",\n      \"priority\": 1,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [\n        \"bug\",\n        \"testing\",\n        \"ralph\"\n      ],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KHF2BK\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Revisit ralph wrap-up agent design and test coverage\",\n      \"description\": \"PR #369 added a wrap-up agent that runs on ralph loop exit. Retrospective flagged it as over-engineered but the intent is broader than simple cleanup: it ensures all work is completed, finds in-progress work where task state doesn't match reality, root-causes whether work is still needed, and does best-effort to get the project into a clean state (either continue the loop or put work on a branch with a task for the user). Too many possible states to rely on code alone — the agent approach is intentional. However: runWrapUpAgent() has zero integration tests (all 37 tests only check prompt strings and boolean helpers). Revisit AC coverage, add integration tests for the actual agent spawn/timeout/cleanup paths, and verify the prompt adequately covers the intended scenarios.\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KHF2BN\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Create spec for validate --drift feature\",\n      \"description\": \"PR #362 added kspec validate --drift, a user-facing CLI flag for AC schema field validation. This was shipped without a spec item or formal ACs, violating the spec-before-code rule. Create a spec item with acceptance criteria covering: field detection from prose, conceptual vs schema fields, strict mode, exit codes, and false positive handling.\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KHF34K\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Add code-level reflect gating in ralph based on iteration delta\",\n      \"description\": \"PR #357 added skill-file instructions to gate reflection on meaningful work, but this has no enforcement. Instead: ralph should snapshot session state (task statuses, working tree, commit count) before each iteration, compare at the end, and only issue the reflect prompt if something measurably changed (task transitions, commits, file changes). The reflect prompt itself was already efficient at avoiding noisy observations — the issue is invoking it at all when nothing happened.\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KHVMWP\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Write getting-started tutorial and README for external users\",\n      \"description\": \"kspec has no end-to-end tutorial for new users. INSTALL.md covers setup mechanics but doesn't show the workflow. README.md is either missing or developer-focused on the kspec project itself, not on using kspec as a tool.\\n\\n## What's needed\\n\\n**README.md** — Public-facing, explains:\\n- What kspec is (spec-first task management for AI-assisted development)\\n- Why (shadow branch, spec-driven workflow, agent integration)\\n- Quick install and init\\n- Link to getting-started tutorial\\n\\n**Getting-started tutorial** (docs/getting-started.md or similar):\\n- Walk through from 'npm install -g' to first completed task\\n- Create a spec item with acceptance criteria\\n- Derive a task from the spec\\n- Work the task (start, implement, note, submit)\\n- Create a PR with kspec trailers\\n- Complete the task\\n- Show the spec-first loop in action\\n\\n**Reference points:**\\n- kynetic-bot, imgen, comfy-ecaj-nodes are real consumer projects showing actual usage patterns\\n- All three independently converged on the same Quick Start: kspec init → kspec setup → kspec session start\\n- The workflow skills (task-work, pr, spec) contain detailed command references that the tutorial can link to rather than duplicate\\n- INSTALL.md already covers setup mechanics — tutorial should reference it, not repeat it\\n\\n## Scope boundaries\\n- README is for the npm package / GitHub repo landing page\\n- Tutorial is for humans AND agents onboarding to a new kspec project\\n- Don't duplicate skill content — link to skills for detailed command syntax\\n- Keep it practical with real examples, not abstract descriptions\",\n      \"priority\": 2,\n      \"spec_ref\": null,\n      \"tags\": [],\n      \"unlocks\": 0\n    }\n  ],\n  \"blocked_tasks\": [],\n  \"recently_completed\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ1G6\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Web UI triage page: add filter controls for triage action types (promote, delete, defer, spec-gap, d\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-01T05:18:14.437Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #619 (commit f42cf881a6469b63d998d87765b2a9fb03c47915): added triage action-type filter control on web UI triage page, wired action filtering into derived card list, and reset card index on action/tag/status filter changes. Added AC-7 E2E coverage for action-filter behavior and stability retry on fallback reload. Reviewed spec alignment and AC coverage (own ac-1..ac-8 plus inherited @trait-websocket-protocol annotations/coverage) with no MUST-FIX or SHOULD-FIX findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ1D\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"ULID short ref ambiguity in batch operations: when two ULIDs share a prefix (e.g. 01KJ4SNE9 and 01KJ\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-01T02:44:56.320Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #618. Implemented shortest-unique ULID display refs across CLI/export and reused shared refs helper for export paths in fix cycle 1. Review verified spec alignment for unambiguous copy-pasteable refs and confirmed @batch-exec own + inherited trait AC annotation coverage. CI checks passed on head 691228e72.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ1E\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Triage promote action should optionally delete the inbox item after creating the task. Currently pro\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-01T01:51:51.959Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #617. Implemented promote consume-by-default behavior in triage act, added --keep escape hatch, and updated dry-run messaging to indicate delete vs keep. Verified AC coverage for @triage-cli-commands (ac-1..ac-17) including new consume/keep scenarios and trait coverage checks; CI checks passed on head 791ea48.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ1CT\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Agents should check plan_ref when starting tasks. If a task has plan_ref, run kspec plan get @plan-r\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-01T01:28:19.393Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #616. Added explicit plan_ref context retrieval guidance to task-work skill (CLI lookup + Start Task step), and regenerated kspec-agents.md. Task has no spec_ref, so AC coverage is N/A; review and CI gates passed on current PR head.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJKBB9\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Fix ralph loop OOM — O(1) seq assignment + event logging backpressure\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-01T01:11:41.050Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #615. Implemented O(1) next-seq derivation for session events via bounded tail read with full-scan fallback in src/sessions/store.ts, and added bounded sequential backpressure queueing for session update logging in src/cli/commands/ralph.ts to prevent unbounded in-flight appendEvent calls. Added/updated tests in tests/ralph.test.ts and tests/sessions.test.ts including explicit AC coverage for @cli-ralph ac-27 and @session-events ac-2; AC coverage audit confirms @cli-ralph ac-1..ac-27 covered.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJK9DV\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Fix ACP RPC parse errors — compact subagent prompts + split budget constants\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-01T00:48:48.299Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #614. Switched subagent prompt context to compact task/spec identity summaries with CLI fetch commands, split prompt budgets to 16KB subagent and 32KB worker, and pinned worker truncation to explicit worker budget. AC coverage for @ralph-subagent-spawning (ac-1..ac-13) verified via annotated tests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ1C2\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Plan import --update replaces all ACs instead of merging. When extending an existing spec with a new\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-03-01T00:04:41.946Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #613. Implemented AC-merge-by-id for plan import --update so existing acceptance criteria are preserved, same-id ACs are replaced in place, and new IDs are appended. Added regression coverage for mixed update+append, omitted acceptance_criteria preservation, empty-existing AC population, and explicit ac-37 annotation coverage. Verified with full npm test and green CI checks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ1A\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Ralph event handler iteration attribution should use session-scoped mapping instead of shared mutabl\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:39:21.126Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #612. Replaced shared sessionIterationMap attribution with session-scoped update logger closures plus explicit detach/replace cleanup on session rotation/end/dispose to prevent listener accumulation while preserving correct late-update iteration attribution. Added regression coverage for session-bound logging and listener replacement ordering in tests/ralph.test.ts. AC coverage for @cli-ralph remains fully annotated (ac-1..ac-26) with no trait ACs.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ17W\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Ralph loop needs iteration-level timeout. When a spawned agent gets stuck (e.g., tool call hanging o\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:14:18.000Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #610. Implemented iteration-timeout hardening by capturing runIterationPrompts() promise and attaching catch before Promise.race to prevent Node.js 22 unhandled rejection on timeout/dispose path. Added/confirmed @cli-ralph ac-24/ac-25/ac-26 for iteration-timeout defaults, validation, and iteration.timeout event behavior, with AC annotations in tests/ralph.test.ts. Verified @cli-ralph AC annotation coverage across ac-1..ac-26 and green PR CI on merge commit 3935ca808c131813871ec5a48e7550f9a239a5a1.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"01KJDQ1B\",\n      \"slug\": null,\n      \"title\": \"Plan import warnings treated as errors in batch mode. The no YAML code block in specs section warnin\",\n      \"completed_at\": \"2026-02-28T23:05:33.314Z\",\n      \"closed_reason\": \"Merged in PR #609. Fixed batch-mode plan import by replacing process.exit(EXIT_CODES.SUCCESS) with return in plan-import.ts success path, preventing BatchExitError interception. Added regression test in batch-exec-engine.test.ts covering warning-only plan import succeeds in batch (ac-34, ac-23). All CI checks passed.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recent_commits\": [\n    {\n      \"hash\": \"f42cf88\",\n      \"full_hash\": \"f42cf881a6469b63d998d87765b2a9fb03c479